@* Spike code (Blazor edition, stage B2): navigation for the static SSR public surface. Links inside the public surface use
   enhanced navigation; the link into the authenticated surface opts out, so crossing the boundary is a full document load. Every href is absolute: under base-uri 'none' the browser resolves a native
   (non-enhanced) link against the document URL, so a relative href breaks on any route below the first segment. *@
<nav data-testid="public-nav">
    <a href="/blazor/" data-testid="nav-landing">Home</a> |
    <a href="/blazor/login" data-testid="nav-login">Log in</a> |
    <a href="/blazor/signup" data-testid="nav-signup">Sign up</a> |
    <a href="/blazor/legal/terms" data-testid="nav-terms">Terms</a> |
    <a href="/blazor/app" data-enhance-nav="false" data-testid="nav-app">Open the app</a>
</nav>
